<title>TUNISIA: Shipping link starts between Tunisia, Egypt, Saudi.</title>
<headline>Shipping link starts between Tunisia, Egypt, Saudi.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Tunisian and an Egyptian shipping company said on Wednesday they had started a regular service to link Tunisian, Egyptian and Saudi ports and increase trade.</p>
<p>The Tunis-based Arab Company for International Trade and Alexandria-based Med Sea said in a statement the 3,000-tonne cargo ship Uni Yamani this week began its first trip, leaving the Tunisian port of Gabes for Alexandria.</p>
<p>From there it will continue to the Saudi port of Jeddah.</p>
<p>- Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
